# repo-paths — system-id -> live repo path locator for `curate/reconcile.py`
#
# Copy this file to `repo-paths.local` (gitignored) and map each managed system's
# id to where its live repo actually lives on THIS machine. reconcile.py reads the
# mapped path DIRECTLY (it does not walk to find it), so a system whose repo is not
# under a `reconcile-roots.local` search root still reconciles.
#
# Why this exists: without it, a system whose repo isn't under a walk root (say, one
# kept in some other folder) shows up as UNLOCATED, and UNLOCATED was repeatedly
# misread as "never onboarded". With the map, UNLOCATED means only "not reachable from this
# machine — add it here," never "not onboarded."
#
# Why a separate gitignored file: machine-specific filesystem paths stay out of
# tracked files (P3 — data/system separation). reconcile.py never stores them.
#
# Format: `<system-id> = <absolute repo path>`, one per line. Split on the FIRST
# `=`, so the path may contain spaces and `=`. The
# system-id is the same id as `inputs/<id>-arch.md` (drop the trailing `-arch`)
# and the system's own STATUS.md `id:` field. Blank lines and `#` comments ignored.
#
# USE THIS MACHINE'S OWN VIEW — the same repo has different paths per machine
# (see reconcile-roots.example). A .local carrying another machine's paths resolves
# nothing and reports every mapped system BROKEN MAP.

# Examples (hypothetical members):
#   example-app = /Users/you/Some Folder/Example App
#   example-tool = /Users/you/Work/example-tool
